  "limits": [
    "The original wrapper matrix supplies empty heaps, pause gates and identity-sign choices; these are explicitly forced inputs.",
    "Public primary/presentation selectors, spans, ordinary movement and menu pause are observed; no secondary gameplay-agent implementation is invented.",
    "A current host batch completes after pause entry. Settled pause retains both clock words; the observer does not assume an immediate entry-hook freeze.",
    "0.6/0.8/1 rates preserve fixed5-ms primary integration. Engine server frames remain100-ms simulation frames; no claim that host rendering or network batching cadence is identical to retail.",
    "Game speed is saved in version168. Other existing frozen trajectory expectations are unchanged; corrected FAST3 round-trip expectation is separately supported by original and public retail evidence.",
    "Earlier unresumed Pause-key and incomplete test-rig attempts are diagnostic only, retained in the external archive."
